{"data":{"attachmentkeynames":["rs"],"desc":"\"Start a new working branch from master.\" Compound and transactional: fetch --prune -> checkout the default branch (master, else main) -> merge --ff-only origin/<default> (a diverged local default is an error to see, never papered over) -> checkout -b <branch> -> push -u origin <branch>. Cuts from the REMOTE's default, never from wherever HEAD is, so an abandoned branch's commits cannot leak into the next one; publishes at birth so the sweeper can push from the first commit. Uncommitted edits are not a blocker: git refuses a switch that would overwrite one (reported verbatim, nothing changed - you stay on the current branch), and the rest ride into the new branch untouched, reported as `carried` (Cargo.lock, rewritten by every build, is the standing case). Refuses an existing branch name, the default branch name, conflicts, or a merge in flight. Returns {status, msg, branch, default, base (short sha), fetched, published, publish_err, carried, steps}.","import":"use ndata::dataarray::DataArray;","params":[{"name":"repo","type":"String"},{"name":"branch","type":"String"}],"returntype":"FLAT","type":"rust"},"id":"ymlwwx1a0733d3513t9","readers":[],"time":1788647669873,"username":"system","writers":[]}